{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Round 1 PASSED and signed at d74d53a5ffd with 0 blocking, but both of its dropped findings were correct and the vetoes were wrong. Verified each against the tree before acting.\n\nFinding 1, dropped as veto:cited-reference-inaccurate. The plan cited CHANGELOG.md:371 for the REBAR_LLM_MODEL v0.12.0 removal. Measured: :371 is issue_count/counted prose; the ## [0.12.0] - 2026-08-15 heading is at :543 and the removal entry at :569. The plan's own citation was also internally impossible, since :371 precedes the :543 heading it claimed to sit under.\n\nFinding 2, same veto. The plan cited docs/release-notes.md:84-91 and CHANGELOG.md:65-75 for the 0092 reconcile-compatibility-adapter removal. Measured: :84-91 is the REBAR_CONFIG_UNKNOWN_KEYS tombstone and CHANGELOG :65-75 is REBAR_HLC rollback plus 429 retry. The real anchors are docs/release-notes.md:833 and CHANGELOG.md:213.\n\nBoth corrected in the description.\n\nMy earlier pre-sweep comment on this ticket said the cites were re-measured and all resolve. That was an overclaim: I verified the ADR citations individually and did not check the CHANGELOG or release-notes evidence citations. The re-measured note now states which set was checked.\n\nThe ADR citations themselves stand: 0021:3, 0020:3,47-48, 0029:5, 0083:5-6, 0092:24-27 and its 56-line length all resolve as cited."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793475880822186001,"uuid":"8f9dc063-c20b-4760-8c7f-27d559c4d6d3"}